  image `pihole -a adlist del https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts`
  does NOT delete the row. It prints "Error: stepping, FOREIGN KEY constraint
  failed (19)" and still exits 0 (V-9). gravity.gravity.adlist_id REFERENCES
  adlist(id) with no ON DELETE action, the image's 165,493 gravity rows
  reference adlist 1, and `pihole-FTL sqlite3` enforces foreign keys
  (PRAGMA foreign_keys = 1). Reproduced on a copy of the image's gravity.db:
  `DELETE FROM adlist WHERE id = 1` -> rc 19; after
  `DELETE FROM gravity WHERE adlist_id = 1` the same delete -> rc 0. The web
  UI's delete (groups.php delete_adlist: adlist_by_group, then adlist) runs
  through PHP's SQLite3, where foreign keys are off by default, so it
  succeeds there. The setup therefore reaches WI 5.1's end state with v5's
  own commands in this order: `pihole -a adlist disable <stock URL>`,
  `pihole -a adlist add http://127.0.0.1:8099/baseline.txt harness-baseline`,
  `pihole -g` (a disabled list is neither downloaded nor kept, so its
  gravity rows go), then `pihole -a adlist del <stock URL>`, which now
  succeeds. Result: the adlist table is exactly
  http://127.0.0.1:8099/baseline.txt|enabled 1|status 1|number 3, and
  gravity_count is 3, the known baseline for TC-126.
  Consequence beyond the harness: `pihole -a adlist del` cannot remove any
  adlist that has gravity rows, so remove-adlist through it fails on a real
  v5 host once gravity has run (WI 5.2's T1 tests will show it).

